{
  "name": "CertMasterAI — 2. Download & Scrape Docs",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "node-manual-2",
      "name": "Manual Trigger",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.manualTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [250, 300]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Set the exam codes to download — edit this list as needed\nconst exams = ['AI-102', 'AZ-104', 'AZ-305', 'GH-300', 'AB-100', 'AI-103'];\nreturn exams.map(code => ({ json: { exam_code: code } }));"
      },
      "id": "node-code-2a",
      "name": "Set Exam Targets",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [480, 300]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "batchSize": 1,
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "node-split-2",
      "name": "Process One Exam at a Time",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.splitInBatches",
      "typeVersion": 3,
      "position": [710, 300]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "url": "http://host.docker.internal:8003/api/v1/admin/index-documents",
        "method": "POST",
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "headerParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "Content-Type",
              "value": "application/json"
            }
          ]
        },
        "sendBody": true,
        "contentType": "json",
        "body": "={\n  \"exam_code\": \"{{ $json.exam_code }}\",\n  \"scraped_dir\": \"./data/scraped\",\n  \"clear_first\": false\n}",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 300000,
          "response": {
            "response": {
              "fullResponse": false
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "id": "node-http-2",
      "name": "Trigger Download + Index",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4,
      "position": [940, 300],
      "notes": "Calls the backend to index scraped docs already on disk.\nRun download_docs.py first to populate data/scraped/."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Log the result for each exam\nconst result = $input.first().json;\nconst exam = $('Process One Exam at a Time').first().json.exam_code;\nconst examResult = result.results?.[exam] || {};\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    exam_code: exam,\n    status: examResult.status || 'unknown',\n    chunks_indexed: examResult.chunks_indexed || 0,\n    files: examResult.files || 0,\n    reason: examResult.reason || null\n  }\n}];"
      },
      "id": "node-code-2b",
      "name": "Parse Result",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [1170, 300]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Workflow 2 — Download & Index\n\nTriggers per-exam indexing into ChromaDB.\n\n**Pre-requisite:** Run the download script first:\n```\ncd backend\npython scripts/download_docs.py --all\n```\n\n**What this does:** Calls POST /admin/index-documents for each exam, which reads scraped .txt files, chunks them, embeds them, and stores them in ChromaDB.\n\n**Tip:** Set `clear_first: true` in the HTTP body to wipe and rebuild the collection.",
        "height": 230,
        "width": 380
      },
      "id": "node-note-2",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [250, 520]
    }
  ],
  "connections": {
    "Manual Trigger": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Set Exam Targets",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Set Exam Targets": {
